SUMMARY:Afternoon Tea & Dessert Pairing
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join us for a special Chinese tea and 
 traditional music event. In this one-hour presentation\, we will learn 
 about Chinese gongfu tea\, its cultural significance and mythical origins\, 
 taste three single-origin teas (green\, white\, and oolong)\, and conclude 
 with a guzheng performance. \n\nChinese gongfu tea is a method of brewing 
 tea with time and effort\, allowing us to control the time\, temperature\, 
 and quantity of the brew to maximize the tea’s flavor. It encourages us 
 to slow down a moment in our day\, to focus on what’s in the cup\, and 
 appreciate what nature can create. Registration is required. \n\n\nMarjorie 
 Wang grew up in NJ\, and attended university in Shanghai\, where she fell 
 in love with Chinese teas. After an apprenticeship at NYC's Tea Drunk\, she 
 began sharing her passion with local communities through tea tasting events 
 at libraries\, community centers\, and clubs. She has been playing the 
 guzheng since age 12\, and continues to perform at local cultural events.
LOCATION:Bloomfield - Theater\, Bloomfield Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Bloomfield Library":MAILTO:reference@bloomfield.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Special Event
UID:LibCal-10270-17334119
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17334119
END:VEVENT
